    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the highest score of the day at 80.17. Facing McGreevy (xERA 4.43), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive \"Order #1\" efficiency boost (+10%) and a favorable platoon matchup, making him our primary engine for both stolen bases and runs. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.63) also presents as a premier start; his 14% dynamic platoon bump against Melton is the most significant situational advantage in our starting nine, effectively neutralizing any concerns regarding the matchup\u2019s SP skill level. While **Gabriel Moreno** (61.24) sits in that same high-tier category, his value is bolstered by his premium slot in the #3 hole, which provides the necessary volume to justify his start despite a slight park penalty.\n\nOur decision-making process at the fringes remains laser-focused on efficiency, particularly given the league's heavy emphasis on stolen base scarcity. **Zach McKinstry** (52.92) gets the nod today despite a lower-middle-order position because the matchup against Dobnak (xERA 5.65) is too favorable to ignore, offering the highest SP skill boost on the board (+19%). Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** (44.49) remains a marginal start, saved only by his positive platoon edge against Bradley; had he been facing a stronger southpaw, we likely would have pivoted to a depth piece like **Jose Caballero** or **Brice Turang** for their superior speed-based upside. \n\nRegarding bench decisions, the landscape is currently barren due to off-days for several of our high-upside assets, including **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. This lack of flexibility makes today a \"load management\" day where we are essentially forced to run our active depth. We are closely monitoring the status of **Austin Riley** (54.41), whose moderate score against Hart reflects the difficulty of facing a lefty; should the lineup reports indicate any late-hour changes or unfavorable stadium wind conditions, we have to keep a watchful eye on potential pinch-hit risks for **Mickey Moniak** or **Giancarlo Stanton** to ensure our game caps are not wasted on sub-optimal plate appearances.",
